---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { repo, supportEmail } from '../lib/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Security"
  description="How OpenMinutes protects what you store, and how to report a vulnerability."
>
  <h2>Report a vulnerability</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> with what you found and how to
    reproduce it. Please do not open a public issue for a security problem. We will reply, fix it
    and credit you if you want.
  </p>

  <h2>How the software is built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Secrets encrypted at rest.</strong> Provider keys, OAuth tokens and the bot's Google
      session are stored encrypted with <code>OPENMINUTES_SECRET</code> and never shown again after
      saving.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No telemetry.</strong> Nothing leaves your server unless you configure a provider.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Open source.</strong> Every line is on <a href={repo}>GitHub</a> under the AGPL-3.0
      for you to read and audit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A visible bot.</strong> It joins under its own name and never hides from participants.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The site is static, served over HTTPS by Cloudflare, with no cookies and no third-party scripts
    except the bot check on the hosting form. The form endpoint is a small Cloudflare Worker that
    forwards your message to our support system and keeps no copy.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosted instances</h2>
  <p>
    Each hosted instance is a separate deployment, served over HTTPS, with backups. Details such as
    access controls and the backup schedule will be listed here before launch.
  </p>
</Legal>
